--!strict
--[[
	Blade Arts (section 8). Every row of the section 8 table, keyed by "<WeaponCategory>.<ArtName>"
	with the name's spaces removed. Axe and Mace share the table's rows, so each appears twice.
	Martial Arts, Shield and Aegis Blade have five original Arts each in the same shape.

	Columns straight from the table: unlock (proficiency 0..1000), hits, startup (seconds; includes
	the 0.15 s start pose and 0.1 s activation hold), total (seconds from input to the last hit),
	postMotion (the lock after the last hit). The rest is tuning:

	- multiplier: damage per hit against weapon attack. A tier-1 single hit is about 1.0; multi-hit
	  Arts split a larger total across their hits so an Art's whole value rises with its unlock;
	  ultimates carry the largest totals.
	- gaugeDamage: Guard Gauge points per hit. Vertical, the two-handed and axe/mace rows and
	  Breaker-style Arts are heavy; a tier-1 arc is about 20.
	- rootMotion: studs the body travels during execution (thrusts 6, Sonic Leap 14, Flashing
	  Penetrator 20, Twin Lance 8, dashes per their notes, arcs 0 to 3).
	- clip: "player/<WeaponCategory>/<ArtName>"; every row maps to one clip module.
	- preconditions: the stance the pose system needs to pick this Art when Arts share a key.

	Rows are plain data; helpers sit at the bottom.
]]

local Types = require(script.Parent.Parent.types)

export type ArtEffect =
	"Launch"
	| "Knockdown"
	| "Knockback"
	| "Pull"
	| "Trip"
	| "Teleport"
	| "Area"
	| "Pierce"
	| "Guard"

export type Art = Types.ArtDef & {
	status: Types.StatusKind?, -- status applied on hit (Quadruple Pain bleeds, Venom Fang poisons)
	effect: ArtEffect?, -- what the hit does to the target beyond damage
}

